The coordinatewise order on compatible sequences holds when every coordinate of the first sequence lies below the corresponding coordinate of the second. The abbreviation is reducible, so it agrees definitionally with that pointwise relation. `inverseLimitLE.refl` says the order is reflexive, because at every stage the coordinate lies below itself. `inverseLimitLE.trans` says it is transitive, because at every stage the coordinate inequality is transitive. `inverseLimitLE.antisymm` says it is antisymmetric: if each sequence lies below the other, then at every stage the two coordinates are equal, so the underlying functions agree and the sequences are equal.
